c(31, "§3.3 P8; §3.4 N4", "monetization", "P8 monetization positives — U:money_positive 5 (7.04%, 5.00★) contradict a naive reading of Part 5: 'the price is just right'; 'really affordable compared to others — definitely like great value'; 'Great app great value'; 'The one time purchase rather than a subscription model is also a lovely thing'; 'basic function still worth using it'. 14 money complaints vs 5 compliments — and N4 price level is only 2 (2.82%, mean 3.00★: 'just wastage of funds', 1★; 'a little bit pricey', 5★) against 7 who object to how much is behind the wall (N1, 2.86★): 'the corpus says the price is broadly acceptable and the boundary is not' — a structure problem, not a pricing problem.", "price acceptable; boundary not", "mixed", "money_positive 5 / 5.00★; MON_PRICE_LEVEL 2 / 3.00★; MON_PAYWALL_BLOCKS 7 / 2.86★", "product-rule", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["13019604470", "12905347299", "13410412793", "13941527190", "14343374736", "13200826254"], "", "")

c(32, "§3.4 N1", "monetization", "N1 'everything is paid' — MON_PAYWALL_BLOCKS 7 (9.86%, mean 2.86★, CI 4.9–19.0%), the single largest negative code; three of six 1★ carry it; 'What's the point of making a free app if it's unfunctional unless you buy a premium plan' (1★); 'only a tiny bit of the app's uses are free' (3★); 'most features require the pro subscription' (5★); 'can only add 1 habit then after that this subscription keeps popping up' (1★); 'You have to pay for widgets' (1★); 'you can't really explore the app' (4★); 'oh the payments wall is hard' (5★) — spread across 6 storefronts and 17 months: persistent, not a spike.", "most features paid; 1-habit free", "blocked-conversion", "7 / 9.86% / 2.86★; 3 of 6 1★; 6 storefronts; 2025-04-11 → 2026-09-05", "product-rule", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["13307114320", "14359876847", "14513739389", "13349206242", "13277885578", "12530006457", "14401503295"], "", "")

c(33, "§3.4 N2; §7.5", "monetization", "N2 the one-habit free cap — U:cap_any 4 (5.63%, 2.50★); all four fall in the second half of the corpus (2025-11-03 → 2026-07-27) — consistent with the cap having tightened and equally with it having become more visible as the base grew.", "1-habit free cap", "blocked-conversion", "4 / 5.63% / 2.50★; all in H2", "product-rule", "High-priority", "generalisable", ["13349206242", "14080954809", "14355567891", "14209508686"], "", "")

